In 'Questions and Answers Web Edition Rev 0 9', dukkha is discussed in this context: *"There are two; 
the first is  sukhan’ti pi vijānāti, dukkhan’ti pi vijānāti, 
adukkhamasukhan’ti pi vijānāti."* Here, dukkha (suffering (dukkha)) is treated not as a theoretical doctrine, but as a living faculty to be actively cultivated and observed. When we bring genuine mindfulness to our direct experience, the quality of dukkha helps dismantle habitual delusion and stabilizes the mind in clear, unentangled awareness.
